# weaver-web lifecycle verbs (Spec section 11). Install as
# /etc/sudoers.d/weaver-web (mode 0440, visudo -c to verify).
# The one privilege widening the application asks of the box.
#
# Wrapper shape (recommended, issue #337): the widening is exactly one
# root-owned script that validates its verb and agent and fixes the
# config itself. Pair with admin_bin = the wrapper and
# admin_env = false in connector.toml.
todd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/weaver-web/weaver-admin-verb *

# Direct-binary shape (wider: arbitrary trailing arguments and the
# config through sudo's environment - what "narrow" overstated until
# the wrapper existed). Uncomment only if not using the wrapper.
#todd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/weaver/weaver-admin validate *, /usr/local/libexec/weaver/weaver-admin load *, /usr/local/libexec/weaver/weaver-admin unload *
#Defaults!/usr/local/libexec/weaver/weaver-admin env_keep += "WEAVER_ADMIN_CONFIG"
